A newly trained Knight walks into the dungeon believing she will be
one of the select few who have managed to escape its dangers, emerging
victorious with the fabled Amulet of Yendor in hands. She throughfuly
explores the first four floors of the mazes until finding the
staircase for the mines, and after whacking many gnomes and getting to
experience level seven Fenrir and her trusty warhorse named Selan
return to the main dungeon in search of a fountain. A hand emerges
from the murky depths and the troughfuly rusty +1 longswords is
transformed into the rustproof Excalibur.

Due to her intelligence of nine, Fenrir makes some epic mistakes in
Sokoban that required of many a wand of striking and squeezing between
non-diagonally-rolling boulders resulting in a luck to give *anyone* a
heart attack. Nevertheless, against all odds she does make it to the
top level and gets some $, a /oCM and "oR for her efforts. Without
doubting, she goes back to the second dungeon level, which contained a
co-aligned altar, to fix her luck somewhat.

After this, it gets pretty much like your average dungeon exploration
story; Fenrir eats an unicorn sandwich, gets poison resistance and
unihorn, a yeti pie and gets cold resistance, water nymph salad grants
teleportitis, tinned tengu teleport control, and so on. She goes to
Mines End and gets the luckstone from there... anyways, the fun starts
when at level fifteen she finds a bones file with a BoH, a magic
marker and a blessed +3 GDSM. She enchants her Excalibur to a +6
capable of yawning at jabberwocks-- but then she gets too greedy...
the idea of getting a +7 is irresistible for her, and therefore she
has another blessed scroll of weapon enchanting.

"Your Excailbur glows violently silver for a while, and then
evaporates!" No... crap... with a squeal, the now un-armed Fenrir
flees from the three jabberwocks and the lich pursuing her (do
remember she had an intelligence of nine!). She returns to her stock
level near the coaligned altar, which she discovers a  dwarf has made
some nice expansions and now also contains a not so peaceful
leocrotta, which she deals with using her lance while mounted on the
warhorse Selan, then sacrificing its corpse and getting a clover in
return. At this point, the player decides the evaporation of Excalibur
might have been related to the last ?oEW she read. Hm, Artifacts
evaporate... interesting.

Anyway, not everything is lost for Fenrir, who advances her lance
skills to expert and manages to get the Frost Brand from Lugh. In the
big room, she finds a brown pudding, and unable to resist the
temptation, she wields that one throughfuly rusty, throughfuly
corroded -3 knife called Puddingbane she got from a bones file and
starts bashing the monsters with that, eventually getting one of the
puddings deliberately jumping into a polymorph trap and becoming a...
prepare yourself... arch lich! It was the revenge of the puddings
alright, but with Selan and expert lance skill Freddy the arch lich
goes down in no time.

After the big scare in the big room, Fenrir does the Quest and beats
the stuffing out of dragon Ixoth, whom with his last breath manages to
curse Selan's saddle. She digs past Medusa's floor, and finds a temple
with a priest of Mannan Mac Lir. After quaffing from some fountains,
water sprouts out of and our Knight somehow manages to confuse the
blue ','s with the safe white '.'s, Fenrir drowns her trusty warhorse
and loses any protection points she had.

The Knight goes back to the mines and finds a pick axe, then she uses
the last charge of her /oC to freeze the ice and dig out the saddle.
Without a mount she attempts the castle; there she fitghts a master
lich, a lich, a demilich, and another lich along with many soldiers
and some olog hai. Having blown up the drawbridge, she zaps the pair
of cursed -2 boots of levitation with her wand of cancellation and
floats over the moat. Finding the /oW, her first wish are two blessed ?
oC. She returns to her stash and builds some protection points,
getting crowned and obtaining the +0 Demonbane. Unfortunately, Fenrir
had no idea wishing resetted her praying timeout and loses all
protection points once more trying to obtain some holy water from
Lugh. She had wished for a blessed figurine of a ki-rin that she calls
My Little Pony and saving her last wish for later, she enters the
Valley of the Dead with a lame AC of -20.

Ki-rin gets turned to stone after five minutes, and Fenrir has to
resolute to her last charge of her /oW for a blessed +oFtS, engraving
Elbereth with the +3 athame Freddy had dropped, she memorizes the
runes and escapes a tragic demise by reviving her stoned mount and
jousting some balrogs to death. The valley was soon cleared, but then
some wraith read some scrolls of create monster and the whole level
was soon alive with nasties once more. Backed onto a corner, the Hand
of Elbereth had no choice but to resolute to the rubber chicken to
deal with the hordes of elvenkings and minotaurs.

Asmodeus fell in only seven turns, Baalzebub only wanted some money,
Jubilex did not even move; and so Fenrir descends to Orcus town and is
disappointed by the fact that Orcus did not summon Demogorgon. She
kills Orcus and nearly loses her ki-rin to one of these impossible to
see shades. Fenrir decided not to wield a rusty tin opener to give
Vlad a fighting chance, and after nearly getting drowned by a purple
worm spitting her into the moat and greedily blocking all adjacent
squares of solid ground in a floor that thank Elbereth wasn't no
teleport, she descends to the very bottom of the dungeons and marks
the vibrating square with an iron golem's chain.

Aggravated at the demilich aggravating all the monsters in the level,
she zaps a wand of digging and unknowingly steps into a magic portal
wich leads her to the Wizard's tower. Before facing Yendor, though,
Fenrir stupidly wields a cursed silver saber and uses her last blessed
clear potion to uncurse it. She finds a magic marker, and enchants
Frost Brand to +7 and the silver saber to +6, two-weaponing them and
beating the stuffing out of many &s until she gets skilled in it. She
wrests one last charge out of the /oW, and wishes for a blessed +3 GoP
which were neither blessed nor +3 but were GoP alright. Using the last
charges of both magic markers, she starts enchanting the gauntlets of
power... and when she gets them to +4... well, there was this one last
blessed ?oEA, and you know...

"Your gauntlets of power glow violently silver for a while and then
evaporate!" One would have thought that after the Excalibur incident
our charismatic, yet stupid knight (and player!) might have learned
her lesson... But, oh well. Picking up the first random pair of
gauntlets she came across, Fenrir attacked the Wizard's tower, nearly
got killed by an arch lich and his nasties, got her ki-rin named My
Little Pony petrifyed by a cockatrice again, and found a +oP; 'Hey,
look! A spell I totally does not suck at!' The girl exclaimed as a
golden haze enveloped her. Failing innumerable times at casting stone
to flesh until finally getting it right, Fenrir and My Little Pony
showed the Wizard what was what and snatching certain papyrus
spellbook they descended into the secret staircase at the vibrating
square...

Is that place called Moloch's Sanctuary? Fenrir decided to refer to it
as "Lich town." Being greeted by two arch liches and a master lich,
Fenrir faced an endless horde of nasties (but no Demogorgon!). Twenty
vampire lords later, and the Wizard's voice boomed out. Nevertheless,
he seemed to totally ignore the Knight and go battle the High
Priestess of Moloch instead. Their fight never got anywhere, though.
Two thousand and six hundred turns later and nothing would happen; and
therefore, half-dead of boredom, Fenrir fell into fire trap after fire
trap in search for the secret door to the place that would soon become
her grave.

As soon as she came in, the Wizard double troubled and called some of
his pets to his aid. Among the summoned were three arch liches; the
three arch liches immediately summoned nasties and not even the
potions of full healing Fenrir had been saving since the very
beginning of the game could save her when an elvenking hit her with a
potion of paralyzis. In no time she was surrounded by lots of
minotaurs, elvenkings, and all these monsters that don't fear
Elbereth's name; My Little Pony was down to 25 hp with no power left
and kneeled down in the next turn, leaving Fenrir without a mount but
at least not burdened since she managed to get this far without
carrying anything useful in her BoH!

She managed to get away, however, casting protection to get her AC
down to a slightly more respectable -29, she fought her way through
minotaurs and killed a cockatrice-- with its corpse she stoned all
liches, all minotaurs, the Wizard, the High Priestess of Moloch, the
elvenkings, and then finally fell on a pit without even laying her
fingers in the real Amulet for once.

DYWYPY?

Should've worn my levitation boots, but I am nearly sure I was 100%
